WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.982
Embedded devices process input from many
places: UART, SPI, I2C, CAN, USB,

2
00:00:04.062 --> 00:00:07.875
BLE, radio packets, network messages,
sensors, local buttons, update channels,

3
00:00:07.955 --> 00:00:09.669
debug commands, and cloud services.

4
00:00:09.749 --> 00:00:11.351
Some inputs are clearly external.

5
00:00:11.431 --> 00:00:14.748
Others feel internal but still cross trust
or reliability boundaries.

6
00:00:14.828 --> 00:00:18.144
Input should be treated as unverified
until it is parsed and validated.

7
00:00:18.224 --> 00:00:21.098
A frame can be well formed and still too
large, out of sequence,

8
00:00:21.178 --> 00:00:24.328
unauthorized, inconsistent, inappropriate
for the current mode,

9
00:00:24.408 --> 00:00:26.342
or invalid for the current state machine.

10
00:00:26.422 --> 00:00:29.959
Parsing confirms structure; validation
confirms permission and meaning.

11
00:00:30.039 --> 00:00:33.853
Defensive firmware parsers use bounded
buffers, length checks, framing checks,

12
00:00:33.933 --> 00:00:36.752
state validation, timeouts, and clear
rejection behavior.

13
00:00:36.832 --> 00:00:39.484
They avoid panic-prone parsing paths in
firmware flows,

14
00:00:39.564 --> 00:00:43.323
especially where malformed or unexpected
input could disrupt service or device

15
00:00:43.403 --> 00:00:43.900
behavior.

16
00:00:43.980 --> 00:00:45.362
Field relationships matter.

17
00:00:45.442 --> 00:00:47.045
A length may not match the payload.

18
00:00:47.125 --> 00:00:50.606
A command may be valid only after
authentication, pairing, provisioning,

19
00:00:50.686 --> 00:00:51.681
or a mode transition.

20
00:00:51.761 --> 00:00:55.077
A sensor value may be syntactically valid
but physically implausible.

21
00:00:55.157 --> 00:00:58.474
A retry value or timeout may parse but
still exceed operational limits.

22
00:00:58.554 --> 00:01:01.649
A strong Rust pattern is to parse into a
temporary representation,

23
00:01:01.729 --> 00:01:03.000
validate fields and state,

24
00:01:03.080 --> 00:01:06.727
then convert the result into domain types
that represent validated messages.

25
00:01:06.807 --> 00:01:10.731
Downstream code should not keep
reinterpreting raw bytes or raw primitives when the

26
00:01:10.811 --> 00:01:12.580
boundary has already made a decision.
